  "_comment": [
    "The update manifest gui/updater.py fetches. This file is an EXAMPLE — it is not",
    "read by anything. Generate the real one with:",
    "",
    "    python3 tools/build-update-manifest.py v1.1.0",
    "",
    "which writes packaging/update.json for a normal release, or update-beta.json for",
    "one marked as a pre-release on GitHub. Those two belong on the two branches the",
    "app looks at: main carries stable, test carries beta.",
    "",
    "Keys the app actually reads: version, date, summary, notes_url, assets. An asset",
    "with no sha256 is refused rather than installed, so every entry must carry one.",
    "The asset keys are fixed — see ASSET_FOR in gui/updater.py — and macOS is split",
    "by architecture because an arm64 bundle installs fine on an Intel Mac and then",
    "will not launch."
  ],
